  "worked_solution": "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{32}=37.3$, $N=32$, and ${S}_{N}=648$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}648 & =\\frac{32}{2}({a}_{1}+37.3) \\\\ 648 & =16({a}_{1}+37.3) \\\\ \\frac{648}{16} & ={a}_{1}+37.3 \\\\ 40.5 & ={a}_{1}+37.3 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
